<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42283" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Săïs</span></b> , is, f.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σάἱς,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the capital of
				Lower Egypt</i>, now <i>Sa el-Hajar</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 9,
			9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 10, 11, §
			64</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Săītes</span></b> ,
				ae, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σαἱτης,</span>
			<i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Sais</i>,
				<i>Saitic</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(nomos),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					5, 9, 9, § 49</span></i>
			.—In <i>plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Săītae</span></b> ,
				ārum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Sais</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D.
				3, 23, 59</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Săĭ_tĭcus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of Sais</i>, <i>Saitic</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(charta),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					13, 12, 23, § 76</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
